.TH HAMSTERD 1 "September 2026" "hamsterd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hamsterd \- local caching HTTP and HTTPS development proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamsterd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hamsterd
is a forward proxy that caches eligible public downloads. It intercepts HTTPS
using a unique local certificate authority generated on first start. The CA is
not trusted or installed automatically.
.PP
Only complete GET responses with status 200 are cached. Requests containing
credentials, cookies, ranges, or cache-bypass directives are not cached.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Use the specified JSON configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-cacert " path"
Use the specified CA certificate file.
.TP
.BI \-cakey " path"
Use the specified CA private-key file.
.TP
.BI \-listen " host:port"
Override the configured listening address.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hamsterd/config.json
Configuration file. Defaults below
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hamsterd/ca.crt
Generated public CA certificate.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hamsterd/ca.key
Generated private CA key. Do not share this file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/hamsterd/
Cached response objects. Defaults below
.IR ~/.cache .
.SH SECURITY
The default listener is 127.0.0.1:8080. Remote listening must be explicitly
enabled and requires separate network access controls. Trust the generated CA
only in clients intentionally configured to use this proxy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lemmingd (1),
the project README, and SECURITY.md.
